  "solution": {
    "text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 350px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Column I</td>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Column II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>Nylon-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">III</td>\t\t\t<td>Bristles of brush</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>Low density polythene</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">IV</td>\t\t\t<td>Toys</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>High density polythene</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">I</td>\t\t\t<td>Buckets</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>Teflon</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">II</td>\t\t\t<td>Non-stick utensils</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Teflon is&nbsp;a brand name for a synthetic chemical called polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE). Teflon is used to coat a variety of products because it&#39;s waterproof, cuts down on friction, and creates a nonstick surface.</p><p>Nylon 66 is a type of polyamide or nylon. It, and nylon 6, are the two most common for textile and plastic industries. Nylon 66 is made of two monomers each containing 6 carbon atoms, hexamethylenediamine and adipic acid, which give nylon 66 its name.</p>",
